    {
      "id": "mechanism",
      "text": "There are no wings. Tanks hold about 600 liters of compressed air, and ten nozzles let it out. Air blasts one way, so the car gets shoved the other way. It's the same trick rockets use to steer in space. When the nozzles stop, the car comes straight back down.",
